; Unit tests for the mlx components — render to HTML via Fur.to_html (native SSR).
; In their own dir, not inside frontend/ (its route_gen rule + data_only_dirs apps
; would otherwise interfere). Links the components lib directly (it is wrapped false,
; so Counter/Nav/Hero are top-level modules). site_handlers: the Mode-B [Me.view]
; whose personalized SSR frame is the mirror of user_badge's anonymous one.

; (modes byte exe): native .exe is what `fennec test` / @runtest run (execution-bound, native
; wins). The byte .bc + per-module .cmo are what the warm test worker Dynlinks per edit in the
; `fennec dev` loop — see cli/dev/test_worker.ml + cli/dev/worker/. Adding byte costs only a
; bytecode link; it never changes what the native gate runs.
(test
 (name test_components)
 (modes byte exe)
 (modules test_components)
 (libraries fennec.fur fennec.fur.server fennec.pulse.sift site_components site_store site_styles site_handlers))

; BYTE-EXACT HTML oracle for the bare-text migration (manual proof tool, not in the test alias).
; `dune exec` it before + after the .mlx migration; the two dumps must be byte-identical.
(executable
 (name snapshot_html)
 (modules snapshot_html)
 (libraries fennec.fur fennec.fur.server fennec.pulse.sift site_components site_store site_styles site_handlers))
